{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement.not_of_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement.not_of_gap","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroResidueSumEquivalence/archimedean_agreement.lean#L137-L150","doc":"**Inhabitation depends on the data** — which is exactly what the old\n`residual = 0` schema failed to do. Here is data at which the class is\n**refutable**: two pipelines a fixed distance apart, and a tolerance smaller\nthan that distance. No instance exists, and no rewriting of the proof can\nproduce one.\n\nThe old schema admitted no such witness: `⟨0, rfl⟩` closed it for every choice\nof everything, so there was nothing a wrong pipeline could fail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement.nonempty_of_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement.nonempty_of_eq","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroResidueSumEquivalence/archimedean_agreement.lean#L130-L135","doc":"**Not over-corrected**: the class is inhabited when the two pipelines\nliterally coincide. Degenerate data, deliberately — the content is that the\nclass is satisfiable at all, so its emptiness is not what makes it open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement.at_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement.at_braid","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroResidueSumEquivalence/archimedean_agreement.lean#L111-L120","doc":"**Agreement transfers to any single braid.**\n\nExercises both fields, and is the edge the `protonExample` carrier consumes to\nderive its specialisation from the generic conjecture. Its existence is what\nmakes the generic class the stronger statement rather than a parallel one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement.agree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement.agree","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroResidueSumEquivalence/archimedean_agreement.lean#L98-L98","doc":"**The conjecture.** The two pipelines agree on every braid, within `ε`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement.tolerance_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement.tolerance_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroResidueSumEquivalence/archimedean_agreement.lean#L96-L96","doc":"The tolerance is a tolerance: a negative `ε` would make the class empty\nrather than open, which is a different and wrong claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroResidueSumEquivalence/archimedean_agreement.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement","kind":"class","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HabiroResidueSumEquivalence/archimedean_agreement.lean#L78-L98","doc":"**Archimedean agreement (generic instance)**: the Habiro polynomial trace\nevaluates to the Gröbner–Shirshov mass, across all closed braids carrying both.\n\nConjectural class — see\n[`conj:gs-archimedean-agreement-trace`](../../../mass-theory/gs-archimedean-agreement-trace.md).\n\nParameters are the caller's data:\n\n* `Braid` — the index type of closed braids carrying both pipelines;\n* `habiroTraceEval K` — the archimedean evaluation of the Habiro trace;\n* `gbMass K` — the Gröbner–Shirshov mass;\n* `ε` — the certified agreement tolerance.\n\nAn instance **is** the conjecture, for that data. None is provided. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:gs-archimedean-agreement-trace","label":"conj:gs-archimedean-agreement-trace","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gs-archimedean-agreement-trace.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}